  "worked_solution": "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2\\theta ={cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3})={cosh}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+{sinh}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}({cosh}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+{sinh}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3}))|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\frac{2\\cdot 4}{3})-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\frac{2\\cdot 1}{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(\\,sinh\\,(\\frac{8}{3})-sinh\\,(\\frac{2}{3})).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
